                <pb facs="0773" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg653"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">notice of ratification by mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of Mexico to the United States of America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1905-05-22"><hi rendition="#italic">May 22,
                                1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 174.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Honorable Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you,
                    for all pertinent purposes, that on the 1st day of the current month, as the
                    department of foreign relations of Mexico has been pleased to advise me, the
                    Government of the Republic ratified the treaty relative to claims for pecuniary
                    damages and injuries that was signed in the said city of Mexico on the 30th day
                    of January, 1902, by the delegates to the Second International American
                    Conference.</p>
                <p>Accept, honorable sir, the renewed assurances of my very high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Gamboa</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’ Affaires ad
                    Interim.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
